      "type": "note",
      "id": "n1",
      "x": 48,
      "y": 540,
      "text": "the backward pass costs ~2x the forward pass and reuses every value the forward pass computed. That is why activations sit in memory, and why batch size is the first thing that blows up your VRAM.",
